# Files that start a process themselves (tools/check-process-starts.py, docs/PROCESSES.md):
# <path> <count of lines found> <reason>

# The two helpers.
crates/appkit-core/src/child.rs 2 the helper for children of the app
crates/appkit-hub/src/launch.rs 2 the helper for a program of somebody else (it outlives the hub on purpose)

# Programs the person sees, handed over and not owned: the default browser, Neovim in a console of its own, the file manager, the folder dialog.
crates/appkit-hub/src/browser.rs 3 hands a link to the default browser (ShellExecuteW, open, xdg-open)
crates/appkit-hub/src/editor.rs 5 opens Neovim in a visible console, the file manager and the folder dialog

# Not children of a running app: the hub puts itself in the background and stops another hub. Its calls of reg.exe, taskkill.exe and kill are short system tools that have not moved to the helper yet.
crates/appkit-hub/src/background.rs 6 starts the hub itself in the background; reg.exe, taskkill.exe, kill not moved yet
crates/appkit-core/src/registry.rs 1 icacls.exe on the secret file, a blocking call that has not moved to the helper yet

# A test program (it plays a child that starts a process of its own).
crates/appkit-testkit/src/bin/child-probe.rs 1 the probe of the child tests
